<BaseLayout title="Checking engine oil level">
  <h1>Checking engine oil level</h1>
  <p>The 2021 S60 four-cylinder gasoline engines use an electronic oil-level sensor rather than a conventional dipstick. The displayed reading is only reliable when the vehicle has met Volvo's measurement conditions.</p>

  <figure class="diagram">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 660 190" role="img" aria-labelledby="oil-flow-title oil-flow-desc">
      <title id="oil-flow-title">Electronic oil-level check sequence</title>
      <desc id="oil-flow-desc">Drive approximately 30 kilometres, park on level ground, switch the engine off, wait five minutes, and then read the electronic oil-level display.</desc>
      <g fill="#f5f5f5" stroke="#444" stroke-width="1.5">
        <rect x="10" y="38" width="145" height="92" rx="4"/><rect x="175" y="38" width="145" height="92" rx="4"/><rect x="340" y="38" width="145" height="92" rx="4"/><rect x="505" y="38" width="145" height="92" rx="4"/>
      </g>
      <g fill="#222" font-size="15" text-anchor="middle">
        <text x="82" y="72">1. Drive</text><text x="82" y="96" font-size="12">Approx. 30 km</text>
        <text x="247" y="72">2. Park</text><text x="247" y="96" font-size="12">Level surface</text>
        <text x="412" y="72">3. Wait</text><text x="412" y="96" font-size="12">Engine off, 5 min</text>
        <text x="577" y="72">4. Check</text><text x="577" y="96" font-size="12">Center display</text>
      </g>
      <g stroke="#333" stroke-width="2" fill="none"><path d="M155 84 H175 M320 84 H340 M485 84 H505"/></g>
      <text x="330" y="166" fill="#555" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">The vehicle must be level and stationary; the display may say no value is available if conditions are not met.</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>Electronic oil-level measurement conditions summarized from Volvo's owner information.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <ReferencePhoto src="https://www.volvocars.com/media/support-content/img4b4a330b573d9c4ec0a801524b07b5d5_1_--_--_VOICEpnghigh.png" variant="reference-diagram" alt="Volvo 2021 S60 engine compartment overview; callout 6 marks the engine oil filler pipe" caption="Oil filler location in Volvo's 2021 S60 engine-compartment illustration — callout 6" credit="Volvo Cars" source="https://www.volvocars.com/uk/support/car/s60/2021/article/f3e117dc70239324c0a801513d2de23c/" license="Volvo Cars support illustration" />

  <h2>Display the oil level</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Drive the vehicle for approximately 30 km (20 miles) where practical, so the system has an updated reading.</li>
    <li>Park on a level surface, switch off the engine, and leave the vehicle stationary for at least 5 minutes.</li>
    <li>With the vehicle in the appropriate ignition state, use the center display's Car Status app and the oil-level status view described in the manual for the installed software version.</li>
    <li>If the display says the value is unavailable, do not treat that alone as a fault. Recheck after the required conditions have been met.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="note"><strong>Important:</strong> Volvo notes that the system does not detect an oil-level change immediately after oil is added or drained. The car may need to be driven approximately 30 km and then remain on level ground with the engine off for 5 minutes before the displayed level is correct.</div>

  <h2>Adding oil</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the exact oil specification for the installed engine code. The Volvo 2021 S60 table lists 0W-20 VCC RBS0-2AE / Castrol Edge Professional V for the T5 and T6 engine codes shown on the <a href="../fluids/">fluids and capacities page</a>.</li>
    <li>Follow the amount requested by the vehicle message or official procedure; do not guess a large top-up quantity.</li>
    <li>Add oil carefully and avoid spilling it onto hot engine or exhaust components.</li>
    <li>Do not use oil additives and do not overfill.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Important distinction</h2>
  <p>An oil-level warning and an oil-pressure warning are not interchangeable. Low oil pressure can indicate a serious lubrication problem even if the electronic oil-level display appears normal. If an oil-pressure warning appears, stop safely, switch off the engine and arrange recovery/diagnosis.</p>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <p><a href="https://www.volvocars.com/us/support/car/s60/20w46">Volvo Cars — 2021 S60 owner's information</a>. See also Volvo's electronic oil-level measurement guidance for four-cylinder engines in the <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/is/support/car/s60/article/b14387177026a34ac0a801515dd998cb/">Volvo support article for the 2021 S60</a>; confirm the menu wording in the manual supplied for the exact vehicle.</p>
  <h2>2026 oil-service cost estimate</h2>
  <p>A complete oil-and-filter service for a 2021 S60 is typically budgeted at <strong>$160–$205</strong> at a U.S. shop. KBB's 2021 S60 fair-repair range is $161–$204 for its displayed ZIP-code estimate. Oil top-ups are different from a full service; use only the exact engine-approved oil and investigate repeated low-level warnings rather than repeatedly topping off. <a href="https://www.kbb.com/volvo/s60/2021/auto-repair/?repair=oil-change&vehicleid=453403">KBB 2021 S60 oil-change estimate</a>.</p>

</BaseLayout>
